The last seemingly technical detail often hides a battle over standards.
@Openledger  This year’s quiet yet most dangerous move is placed on a protocol called x402—it aims to give your API the ability to handle automatic billing, no emotions, just payments.
The tipping point for this logic isn't now, but on April 2, 2026. The Linux Foundation will take over the governance of the x402 protocol, transferring management from Coinbase to the open-source community. The x402 Foundation, established on the same day, boasts a founding member list that reads like a family photo of global tech giants—Google, Microsoft, Amazon Web Services, Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Circle, and the Solana Foundation are all on it.
